# MoveWise — Environment Variables
#
# NOTE: the current index.html prototype is a single self-contained file with no backend
# and no live API calls — all transport data (stations, bus routes, exits) is embedded
# directly as static JavaScript. None of the variables below are read by that file today.
#
# This template documents what would be needed to wire MoveWise up to the real data
# sources named in README.md (LTA DataMall, OneMap, weather, Google Cloud), for whenever
# that integration is built. Copy this file to `.env`, fill in real values, and never
# commit `.env` itself.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LTA DataMall
# Powers: TrainServiceAlerts, BusArrival, BusServices, BusRoutes, BusStops,
# PCDRealTime, PCDForecast, v2/FacilitiesMaintenance, TrainStation,
# TrainStationExit, BusStopLocation, CoveredLinkWay, CyclingPath, Footpath
# Request a free AccountKey at: https://datamall.lta.gov.sg/
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
LTA_DATAMALL_ACCOUNT_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OneMap (Singapore Land Authority)
# Powers: geocoding, reverse geocoding, walking/cycling/public-transport routing
# Register at: https://www.onemap.gov.sg/apidocs/
# OneMap tokens are typically obtained via email/password login rather than a
# static key — store whichever credentials your integration actually uses.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
ONEMAP_EMAIL=
ONEMAP_PASSWORD=
ONEMAP_API_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# data.gov.sg — Weather
# Powers: rain/weather conditions used to inform walking & cycling last-mile options
# Most data.gov.sg datasets (e.g. realtime rainfall) are open and don't require a
# key — leave blank unless your integration uses an authenticated endpoint.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
DATA_GOV_SG_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google Cloud (deployment target for Nebula X judging)
# Only needed if the app is deployed as a Cloud Run / App Engine / Cloud
# Functions service rather than served as a static file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT_ID=
GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=
PORT=8080

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# App-level config
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# "development" | "production"
NODE_ENV=development
